  "question": "A current of 2 A flows through a resistor of 10 Ω. Calculate voltage.",
  "gold_answer": "# Solved Numerical\n\n---\n\n## Ohm's Law Problem\n\n### Problem\nA steady electric current of $2 \\text{ A}$ flows through a resistor with a value of $10 \\ \\Omega$. Calculate the voltage drop across the resistor.\n\n### Given\n* Current tracking ($I$) = $2 \\text{ A}$\n* Resistance value ($R$) = $10 \\ \\Omega$\n\n### Formula\n$$V = IR$$\n\n### Substitution\n$$V = 2 \\times 10$$\n\n### Calculation\n$$V = 20 \\text{ V}$$\n\n### Final Answer\n**Potential Difference ($V$) = $20 \\text{ V}$**\n\n### Interpretation\nThis means that a potential difference of $20 \\text{ Volts}$ must be maintained across the ends of the $10 \\ \\Omega$ resistor to sustain a continuous current flow of $2 \\text{ Amperes}$.",
  "candidate_response": "<thinking>\nThe user wants to calculate voltage using Ohm's Law. Let me structure this as an interactive textbook with proper UI blocks, formula cards, and sections.\n\nV = I × R = 2 × 10 = 20 V\n\nLet me render this properly with the new rendering system.\n</thinking>\n\n<div style=\"font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n\n<!-- Topic Header -->\n<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e3a5f 0%, #2d6a9f 100%); border-radius: 14px; padding: 28px 32px; color: white;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; opacity: 0.75; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚡ Electricity · Ohm's Law</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Calculating Voltage</div>\n  <div style=\"opacity: 0.85; font-size: 15px;\">Given: Current and Resistance → Find: Voltage</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Quick Definition Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #f0f7ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 26px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #3b82f6; margin-bottom: 10px;\">📘 Quick Definition</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 15px; color: #1e3a5f; line-height: 1.7;\">\n    <strong>Ohm's Law</strong> states that the voltage across a conductor is directly proportional to the current flowing through it, provided temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Formula Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #6366f1; border-radius: 14px; padding: 28px 32px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(99,102,241,0.12);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #6366f1; margin-bottom: 16px;\">📐 Core Formula</div>\n\n  <!-- Rendered Formula -->\n  <div style=\"background: #f5f3ff; border-radius: 10px; padding: 22px; text-align: center; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 20px; border: 1px solid #e0e7ff;\">\n\n$$V = I \\times R$$\n\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Variable Table -->\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #fef9c3; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #fde68a;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: #92400e;\">V</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #78350f; margin-top: 4px;\">Voltage</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #a16207; margin-top: 2px;\">Volts (V)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #dcfce7; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: #166534;\">I</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #15803d; margin-top: 4px;\">Current</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #16a34a; margin-top: 2px;\">Amperes (A)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #fce7f3; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #fbcfe8;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: #9d174d;\">R</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #be185d; margin-top: 4px;\">Resistance</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #db2777; margin-top: 2px;\">Ohms (Ω)</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Given Values Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 26px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #6b7280; margin-bottom: 16px;\">📋 Given Values</div>\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n    <div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 140px; background: #f0fdf4; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; border-left: 4px soli